From 609999f2112d667cf1890de8505330e9e53c1cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BaresipKit <baresipkit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sipsess: session timers (RFC 4028)

sipsess_set_timer() enables session timers for the sessions of a socket: an INVITE offers Supported: timer, Session-Expires and Min-SE, a 2xx to an INVITE whose caller supports timers carries Session-Expires with the refresher and Require: timer, an INVITE or UPDATE whose interval is below Min-SE is answered with 422, and a 422 raises the interval to the peer's Min-SE and sends the request again. The refresher sends an UPDATE without a body at half the interval, or a re-INVITE without an offer when the peer does not allow UPDATE, and ends the session itself when no refresh could be sent before the interval runs out; the other side ends the session with BYE when no refresh arrived in time. sipsess_timer() returns the negotiated interval and whether this side refreshes. Without sipsess_set_timer() nothing changes.
